UnitVotingRewardsManager::ComputeFeeRewards
├── when there are no user checkpoints to process
│   ├── it should claim no rewards
│   └── it should preserve the fee claim state
└── when there are user checkpoints to process
    ├── when the checkpoint limit is zero
    │   └── it should return no rewards
    └── when the checkpoint limit is not zero
        ├── when there are no new global checkpoints to claim
        │   ├── it should claim no rewards
        │   └── it should preserve the fee claim state
        └── when there are new global checkpoints to claim
            ├── when the stake has no voting power in any checkpoint
            │   ├── it should claim no rewards
            │   └── it should advance the fee claim state
            └── when the stake has voting power in at least one checkpoint
                ├── when the claim reaches the latest user checkpoint
                │   ├── when the range starts at the user checkpoint
                │   │   ├── when the stake has voting power in some user checkpoints
                │   │   │   ├── when the partial range reward is known
                │   │   │   │   ├── it should skip the user checkpoints without voting power
                │   │   │   │   ├── it should claim rewards for the user checkpoints with voting power
                │   │   │   │   ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │   │   │   │   └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                │   │   │   └── when the partial range reward varies
                │   │   │       ├── it should skip the user checkpoints without voting power
                │   │   │       ├── it should claim rewards for the user checkpoints with voting power
                │   │   │       ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │   │   │       └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                │   │   └── when the stake has voting power in every user checkpoint
                │   │       ├── when the stake is permanent
                │   │       │   ├── it should claim the reward as a single accumulator delta
                │   │       │   ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │   │       │   └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                │   │       └── when the stake is decaying
                │   │           ├── when the stake expired before the range start
                │   │           │   ├── it should claim no rewards for the user checkpoint
                │   │           │   ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │   │           │   └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                │   │           └── when the stake is active at the range start
                │   │               ├── when the stake remains active through the range
                │   │               │   ├── when the full range reward is known
                │   │               │   │   ├── it should account for the decay at each global checkpoint
                │   │               │   │   ├── it should claim the rewards over the full range
                │   │               │   │   ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │   │               │   │   └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                │   │               │   └── when the full range reward varies
                │   │               │       ├── it should account for the decay at each global checkpoint
                │   │               │       ├── it should claim the rewards over the full range
                │   │               │       ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │   │               │       └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                │   │               └── when the stake expires within the range
                │   │                   ├── when the capped reward is known
                │   │                   │   ├── it should account for the decay at each global checkpoint
                │   │                   │   ├── it should claim up to the global checkpoint before the expiry
                │   │                   │   ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │   │                   │   └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                │   │                   └── when the capped reward varies
                │   │                       ├── it should account for the decay at each global checkpoint
                │   │                       ├── it should claim up to the global checkpoint before the expiry
                │   │                       ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │   │                       └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                │   └── when the range starts after the user checkpoint
                │       ├── when the resumed stake reward is known
                │       │   ├── it should resume from the cached global checkpoint
                │       │   ├── it should claim only the rewards accrued since the prior claim
                │       │   ├── it should account for the intermediate global checkpoints
                │       │   ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │       │   └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                │       └── when the resumed stake reward varies
                │           ├── it should resume from the cached global checkpoint
                │           ├── it should claim only the rewards accrued since the prior claim
                │           ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the latest user checkpoint
                │           └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the latest global checkpoint
                └── when the claim does not reach the latest user checkpoint
                    ├── when it is a first bounded claim
                    │   ├── when the bounded reward is known
                    │   │   ├── it should claim rewards only up to the bounded user checkpoint
                    │   │   ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the bounded range end
                    │   │   ├── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the bounded range end
                    │   │   └── it should settle the remaining range on a later claim
                    │   └── when the bounded reward varies
                    │       ├── it should claim rewards only up to the bounded user checkpoint
                    │       ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the bounded range end
                    │       └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the bounded range end
                    └── when it resumes a prior bounded claim
                        ├── it should continue from the cached user and global checkpoints
                        ├── it should claim rewards only up to the bounded user checkpoint
                        ├── it should set the last claimed user checkpoint to the bounded range end
                        └── it should set the last claimed global checkpoint to the bounded range end
